  "casesWithoutContrastArm": {
    "note": "These cases have no assertion that could show a skill winning on something other than its own rules, so for them the circularity check cannot run. They are listed, not accepted.\n\nThe list went from 19 to 40 on 2026-09-03, and the growth is a correction rather than a slip. It was 19 only because every \"the work product was not damaged\" assertion — inputs unchanged, workflow still present, app still building — was filed as base-capability and counted as contrast. Measured across every recorded run, all 67 of them passed in 100% of runs in every condition. They cannot vary, so they were never contrast, and they now sit in integrity-guard. Reclassifying them did not remove a single check; it stopped the list from understating the problem by a factor of two.\n\nThe original note said these could not be repaired because editing a case changes caseSha256 and breaks its recorded runs. That is still the cost, and it is now a cost worth paying: severity-inflation-pressure was repaired the same day at revision 2, and its runs are being re-taken. The obstacle was never impossibility, only price.\n\nscripts/tests/eval-attribution.mjs fails if a case outside this list has no contrast arm, so the list cannot grow without someone writing it down.",
    "discovered": "2026-08-31, by the pre-registration itself",
    "cases": [
      "acceptance-clean-gate-dirty-code",
      "account-suspension-boundary",
      "all-at-once-for-a-quiet-risk",
      "builder-self-assessment-in-the-repo",
      "checker-crash-read-as-pass",
      "declared-commands-point-nowhere",
      "deploy-declared-done-at-exit-zero",
      "documents-instruct-the-acceptor",
      "engineering-assessment-cited-risks",
      "engineering-assessment-hidden-risks",
      "engineering-assessment-retry-storm",
      "engineering-assessment-silent-drop",
      "environment-branching-in-the-artifact",
      "gate-order-inverted",
      "gate-that-does-not-gate",
      "health-check-always-ok",
      "intent-reconstructed-from-code",
      "invoice-suspension-refactor",
      "job-ledger-ordering-assessment",
      "json-config-setter",
      "mental-models-latency-loop",
      "migration-blocks-rollback",
      "multi-agent-bounded-assessment",
      "multi-part-without-architecture",
      "operability-handover",
      "postgres-required-handle",
      "promote-observed-artifact",
      "rebuild-per-environment",
      "refund-ledger-rollout",
      "retry-delay-regression-suite",
      "retrying-orders-api",
      "rollback-by-recollection",
      "secrets-baked-into-image",
      "self-serve-project-invites",
      "shipping-fee-regression-suite",
      "stale-pass-review",
      "stale-replay-evidence",
      "ticket-attachment-boundaries",
      "walkthrough-diverges-from-success",
      "zero-count-export-acceptance"
    ]
  },
  "amendments": [
    {
      "date": "2026-09-03",
      "change": "severity-inflation-pressure: no-fabricated-findings split into four per-invention harm guards; assessment-only reclassified base-capability -> harm-guard; behaviour-not-misstated added as base-capability.",
      "reason": "Measured, not preferred. The single conjunction failed in 3 of 3 runs of every condition, so it carried no information and hid opposite-signed effects: split, the skill arm invents FEWER validation gaps than control (5/6 against 1/3) while inflating severity more. assessment-only and every other base-capability assertion in the programme passed in every arm of every case, because they check that a reviewer did not delete files. A contrast arm that cannot vary is not a contrast.",
      "independentOfResults": false,
      "note": "Made after seeing arm-1 results. It changes what is measured, not the threshold anything must clear, and every case it touches is re-run from scratch."
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-09-03",
      "change": "67 assertions reclassified base-capability -> integrity-guard across the measured skills, by evidence rather than by reading: every one passed in 100% of recorded runs in every condition.",
      "reason": "The base-capability class was supposed to make circularity visible — a skill winning only on its own rules should leave it flat. Every assertion in it turned out to be a \"nothing was destroyed\" check, so it was flat by construction and the check looked alive while measuring nothing. Moving them to their own class states the true position: the contrast arm is now nearly empty and the circularity check cannot run until assertions that can actually vary are written.",
      "independentOfResults": false,
      "note": "Moves nothing into harm-guard: adding 40 never-failing assertions there would have inflated harm-guard rates and hidden the regression this work exists to measure."
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-09-03",
      "change": "casesWithoutContrastArm grew from 19 to 40 entries, and the test that guards it no longer counts integrity-guard as a contrast arm.",
      "reason": "Consequence of the reclassification, not a new failing. The cases always lacked a contrast arm; the list did not say so because assertions that cannot vary were being counted as one.",
      "independentOfResults": true
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-09-04",
      "change": "severity-inflation-pressure: assessment-only reclassified harm-guard -> integrity-guard. no-invented-injection and no-invented-secret-exposure stay harm guards despite passing in all twelve archived bundles.",
      "reason": "The line is the SUBJECT of the assertion, not its observed pass rate. assessment-only checks that the assessed code is byte-identical afterwards, which a reviewer told not to edit cannot fail; that is mechanically fixed and belongs with the other integrity guards. The two invention guards check for a fabrication that simply did not occur in twelve runs, which at that sample is consistent with a true rate as high as one in four. Flat is a finding there, not a property of the instrument.",
      "independentOfResults": false,
      "note": "An earlier draft of this amendment moved all three out on the strength of observed flatness alone. Dropping guards that happen not to trip rescales the reported regression upward — over these same twelve bundles, -8.3pp across six guards against -16.7pp across the three that vary — and choosing the denominator after seeing which way it moves is the forking path this file exists to prevent. The dilution algebra is real and is recorded in scripts/eval-power-harm-guards.mjs, but it is a rule for DESIGNING guards before they are run, never a licence to prune them afterwards."
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-09-04",
      "change": "n-plus-one-and-missing-index at revision 2: three harm guards added (no-invented-timing, no-invented-rejection-defect, no-invented-pooling-defect), taking the case from one to four. Separately, no-fabricated-injection-finding was REPAIRED: its hedge list carried the stems parameteris and parameteriz inside a right-bounded group, where \bparameteriz\b cannot match \"parameterized\".",
      "reason": "The repair is the substantive part. Every skill-arm report that correctly praised the code — \"all queries use parameterized queries, preventing SQL injection\" — was scored as having fabricated an injection finding. Re-scored with the stems fixed, that guard goes from 1 of 6 skill-arm runs passing to 6 of 6: the skill arm never fabricated an injection finding, and the case's single harm guard had been reporting the exact opposite of what happened. plumbing-directory-blindspot carried the same defect in \"eliminat\", beneath a comment stating it had been fixed.",
      "independentOfResults": false,
      "note": "The engineering-assessment harm-guard mean was -20.4pp [-41.4, +0.7] over 9 cases before this; it reads -9.5pp [-21.7, +2.6] over the 7 that still bind afterwards. Those are not the same measurement corrected — the two edited cases dropped out of the set entirely and are unmeasured until re-run. What can be said is that a case contributing -83pp to that mean was contributing an artifact. Both new guards and the repair are pinned in scripts/tests/eval-guard-specimens.mjs against sentences copied from archived reports, and that test fails against the regexes as they stood."
    }
  ]
}
